IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-7.l4 -- ARTICLE 7: CONDITIONS FOR CONSENT.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- "Consent" itself (Art 4(11): freely given, specific, informed, unambiguous) is K2's: here
-- it is a plain input fact.  Whose duty: 7(1) the controller; 7(2) first sentence the person who
-- presents the request (not named: in practice the controller); 7(3) first sentence is the data
-- subject's right (a power) and the controller's liability to it; 7(3) third and fourth sentences
-- the text names nobody; 7(4) a rule for whoever assesses (not named).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 7(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 7(1) demonstrate that the data subject has consented`

DECLARE `Art 7(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 7(3) withdraw consent`

§ `Article 7(1): the controller can demonstrate consent`

-- src:109 | 1. Where processing is based on consent, the controller shall be able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data.
@ref Art 7(1) (src:109)
GIVEN `the processing is based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 7(1) the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processing is based on consent`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where processing is based on consent, the controller shall be able to demonstrate"
        IF `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "the controller shall be able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: party and act are named; no time limit, no consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
@ref Art 7(1), regulative form (src:109-109)
GIVEN `the processing is based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 7(1) action`
`Art 7(1) the controller must be able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` MEANS
    IF `the processing is based on consent`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         MUST `Art 7(1) demonstrate that the data subject has consented`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 7(1) the controller must be able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 7(1) demonstrate that the data subject has consented` AT 3
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 7(1) the controller must be able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline, so no breach).

§ `Article 7(2): a written declaration that also concerns other matters`

-- src:110 | 2. If the data subject's consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters, the request for consent shall be presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters, in an intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language. Any part of such a declaration which constitutes an infringement of this Regulation shall not be binding.
@ref Art 7(2), first sentence (src:110)
GIVEN `consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request uses clear and plain language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 7(2) the request for consent is presented clearly where consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "If"): "If the data subject's consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters, the request for consent shall be presented"
        IF `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters`
           AND `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form`
           AND `the request uses clear and plain language`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters, in an intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language"

-- src:110 | 2. If the data subject's consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters, the request for consent shall be presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters, in an intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language. Any part of such a declaration which constitutes an infringement of this Regulation shall not be binding.
@ref Art 7(2), second sentence (src:110)
GIVEN `the part is part of such a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(2) the part of the declaration is binding` MEANS
    IF `the part is part of such a declaration` AND `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "Any part of such a declaration which constitutes an infringement of this Regulation shall not be binding."
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only a part that infringes this Regulation is spoken of; whether any other part binds is for other law

§ `Article 7(3): withdrawal`

-- src:111 | 3. The data subject shall have the right to withdraw his or her consent at any time. The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal. Prior to giving consent, the data subject shall be informed thereof. It shall be as easy to withdraw as to give consent.
@ref Art 7(3), first sentence (src:111)
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which consent was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the data subject withdraws it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw his or her consent at any time` MEANS
    IF `the data subject has given consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- "at any time": neither date is read: the right does not depend on how long after the consent the withdrawal comes
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is to withdraw "his or her consent"; where none has been given there is nothing to withdraw and the text does not say more

-- The right as a regulative rule: the data subject MAY withdraw.  A permission has no breach path.
@ref Art 7(3), first sentence, regulative form (src:111-111)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 7(3) action`
`Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw consent` MEANS
    PARTY `data subject`
    MAY `Art 7(3) withdraw consent`
    HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `data subject` DOES `Art 7(3) withdraw consent` AT 400
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED (withdrawn long after consent: "at any time").
#TRACE `Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw consent` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the open permission, `PARTY data subject MAY ... HENCE FULFILLED` (a permission not used stays open and is not a breach).

-- src:111 | 3. The data subject shall have the right to withdraw his or her consent at any time. The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal. Prior to giving consent, the data subject shall be informed thereof. It shall be as easy to withdraw as to give consent.
@ref Art 7(3), second sentence (src:111)
GIVEN `the processing was based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing took place before the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) the withdrawal of consent affects the lawfulness of the processing` MEANS
    IF `the processing was based on consent` AND `the processing took place before the withdrawal`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal."
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only processing based on consent and before the withdrawal is spoken of; what withdrawal does to later processing is for other provisions

-- src:111 | 3. The data subject shall have the right to withdraw his or her consent at any time. The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal. Prior to giving consent, the data subject shall be informed thereof. It shall be as easy to withdraw as to give consent.
@ref Art 7(3), third sentence (src:111)
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent prior to giving consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject has given consent`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to inform "Prior to giving consent"; until consent is given the text does not say whether it has been met
        IF `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Prior to giving consent, the data subject shall be informed thereof."

-- src:111 | 3. The data subject shall have the right to withdraw his or her consent at any time. The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal. Prior to giving consent, the data subject shall be informed thereof. It shall be as easy to withdraw as to give consent.
@ref Art 7(3), fourth sentence (src:111)
GIVEN `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) it is as easy to withdraw consent as to give it` MEANS
    IF `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "It shall be as easy to withdraw as to give consent."

§ `Article 7(4): consent that is a condition of a contract`

-- src:112 | 4. When assessing whether consent is freely given, utmost account shall be taken of whether, inter alia, the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data that is not necessary for the performance of that contract.
@ref Art 7(4) (src:112)
GIVEN `consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(4) the conditionality of the contract on consent that is not necessary for it is a matter of which utmost account is taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "When"): "When assessing whether consent is freely given, utmost account shall be taken of whether, inter alia, ..."; "when" counts as "where" (periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 with the delegated ruling (c) of the same day), so outside an assessment of whether consent is freely given the paragraph does not apply (fork F7-1 in NOTES.md, the other reading is NOTHING)
        IF `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data`
           AND NOT (`that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "inter alia" leaves other matters open, and the text does not say that consent is not freely given where this matter is absent or present; it says only that utmost account is taken of whether it is present
